{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-20-012", "date": "2026-11-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Electronics Announces New Leadership", "content": "Samsung Electronics today announced new leadership for the next phase of the Company’s growth and to strengthen its future competitiveness on the semiconductor business. Sang Joon Hwang was promoted to President and will become the Head of Memory Business, while Sangyeun Cho was also promoted to President and will lead the System LSI Business. Jong […]", "sources": [{"name": "samsung_elec", "url": "https://news.samsung.com/global/samsung-electronics-announces-new-leadership-5", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lg_elec-2026-11-20-013", "date": "2026-11-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "automotive_display"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "LG Display officially cancels its $2.25 billion 10.5-Gen OLED TV line investment at its P10 fab", "content": "<p>LG Display announced that it has officially cancelled its plan to invest around $2.25 billion in a 10.5-Gen OLED TV production line at its P10 fab in Paju, Korea. The company's board decided on November 19 not to go ahead with the investment, which was approved back in July 2019 and has been <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-delays-its-p10-105-gen-oled-tv-fab-2025\">postponed several times</a> since. In our <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/spotlight-lg-display-woled-pioneer-apples-second", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-officially-cancels-its-225-billion-105-gen-oled-tv-line-investment", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-20-014", "date": "2026-11-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["weak", "uncertainty", "[否定]delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Apple weighs delaying or canceling OLED iMac development", "content": "Apple was discussing a delay to its OLED iMac development schedule with Samsung Display and was also considering canceling the project, according to South Korean media reports. The review was driven by high OLED panel costs, weak sales of existing OLED products, and uncertainty over whether an OLED iMac could remain price competitive.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261120PD239/apple-imac-development-sdc-lg-display.html", "type": "rss"}]}
